<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Sai's Vegas &amp; LA Trip</name><Style id="sff4fa3"><IconStyle><color>ffa34fff</color><scale>1.2</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="s3fe0e8"><IconStyle><color>ffe8e03f</color><scale>1.2</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="sffb547"><IconStyle><color>ff47b5ff</color><scale>1.2</scale><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Style id="sx"><IconStyle><color>ffc8a8a8</color><Icon><href>http://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/paddle/wht-blank.png</href></Icon></IconStyle></Style><Folder><name>Sat 24 · Arrival + center Strip</name><description>Free all day</description><Placemark><name>1. Harry Reid Airport (LAS)</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 24: Arrival + center Strip</b><br>10:00 — Land at LAS. Cab to Circus Circus and drop your bags.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Arrive Sat Oct 24, 10:00 AM<br>• Depart Sat Oct 31, 11:59 PM<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Uber/Lyft to the Strip in about 15–20 minutes.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> On the last night, be at the airport by about 9:30 PM.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1537,36.084,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Venetian &amp; Palazzo</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 24: Arrival + center Strip</b><br>11:45 — Deuce to the Venetian: Grand Canal, gondolas, St. Mark's Square. See Sphere from outside.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Indoor Grand Canal with gondolas and singing gondoliers<br>• St. Mark's Square street performers<br>• Right next to Sphere<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Deuce to the Venetian stop.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Good midday stop on Saturday: indoors and cool while you wait for check-in.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1697,36.1212,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Wynn &amp; Encore</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 24: Arrival + center Strip</b><br>1:30 — Walk back north via Wynn's flower lobby.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Flower displays and the carousel sculptures in the lobby<br>• Calm, beautiful walk-through<br><br><b>Get there:</b> About 8 minutes' walk from Fontainebleau.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> An easy Monday-night stroll if you have energy after the bus.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1657,36.1265,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Circus Circus</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 24: Arrival + center Strip</b><br>3:00 — Check in. Sleep 3:30–6 PM; tonight is a short night.<br>10:30 — Back to the hotel to rest. Leave for the bus stop around 1:45 AM.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 1: Sat Oct 24 (3 PM) → Mon Oct 26 (10 AM)<br>• Bell desk holds bags before check-in<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Deuce stop out front. Fontainebleau is a 10-minute walk across the street.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Drop bags on arrival, then rest here 3–6 PM before the overnight bus.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.165,36.1376,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Caesars Forum Shops</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 24: Arrival + center Strip</b><br>6:30 — Deuce south: Forum Shops at Caesars.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Roman-style indoor street with a painted sky<br>• Fall of Atlantis fountain show (free)<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Deuce to Caesars Palace.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Walk from here south to Bellagio in 10 minutes.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1752,36.1178,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>6. Bellagio Fountains</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 24: Arrival + center Strip</b><br>7:30 — Bellagio Conservatory and fountain shows every 15 minutes.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Fountain shows set to music, every 15 minutes after dark<br>• Conservatory: free seasonal fall garden display inside<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Deuce to Bellagio/Caesars stop.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Watch from the bridge in front of Paris, or from the Eiffel Tower deck.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1767,36.1126,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>7. Paris · Eiffel Tower</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 24: Arrival + center Strip</b><br>8:30 — Optional: Eiffel Tower deck over the fountains.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Half-size Eiffel Tower with a viewing deck<br>• Best view down onto the Bellagio fountains<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Across the street from Bellagio.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Optional add-on on Saturday night.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1707,36.1125,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Sun 25 · LA: Universal, Hollywood, sunset</name><description>Free all day</description><Placemark><name>1. Downtown LA bus stop</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun 25: LA: Universal, Hollywood, sunset</b><br>8:15 — Arrive Downtown LA. Quick breakfast.<br>9:00 — Metro E Line from Downtown Santa Monica back toward downtown. Be at the bus stop by 11:45 PM.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Arrive 8:15 AM Sunday<br>• Depart 12:30 AM Monday<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Assumed near Union Station; check your ticket.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Grab breakfast at Union Station or nearby Grand Central Market.]]></description><styleUrl>#s3fe0e8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.2365,34.0562,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Universal Studios Hollywood</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun 25: LA: Universal, Hollywood, sunset</b><br>8:45 — Metro B Line to Universal City. Inside the park by ~9:20.<br>9:20 — Universal no-coaster plan (see below) until 3:00 PM.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Studio Tour of real movie backlots<br>• Super Nintendo World &amp; Wizarding World<br>• Open 8 AM – 6 PM on Oct 25<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Metro B Line to Universal City/Studio City (~25 min), then a short walk or free shuttle up the hill.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> See the full no-coaster plan below.]]></description><styleUrl>#s3fe0e8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.3534,34.1381,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Hollywood &amp; Highland</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun 25: LA: Universal, Hollywood, sunset</b><br>3:15 — B Line one stop to Hollywood/Highland: Sign view, Walk of Fame, Chinese Theatre.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hollywood Sign view from the upper terraces of Ovation Hollywood<br>• TCL Chinese Theatre handprints<br>• Walk of Fame stars<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Metro B Line, one stop from Universal City (~5 min).<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Go to the top-level walkway for the clearest sign photo.]]></description><styleUrl>#s3fe0e8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.3387,34.1017,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Santa Monica Pier</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun 25: LA: Universal, Hollywood, sunset</b><br>4:40 — Cab to Santa Monica Pier.<br>6:05 — Sunset over the Pacific. Pier lights come on.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Sunset over the Pacific about 6:05 PM<br>• Pacific Park Ferris wheel (slow and gentle)<br>• End of Route 66 sign, beach walk<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Cab from Hollywood (~50 min). Back by Metro E Line.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Arrive by 5:30 PM, walk the pier, then claim a spot on the sand.]]></description><styleUrl>#s3fe0e8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.4973,34.0094,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Third Street Promenade</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sun 25: LA: Universal, Hollywood, sunset</b><br>7:00 — Dinner on Third Street Promenade.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Walkable street of restaurants and shops<br><br><b>Get there:</b> 5-minute walk from the pier.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Dinner here, then Downtown Santa Monica station is right next to it.]]></description><styleUrl>#s3fe0e8</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.497,34.016,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Mon 26 · Hotel switch, early night</name><description>Free after 9 PM</description><Placemark><name>1. Circus Circus</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon 26: Hotel switch, early night</b><br>5:50 — Bus arrives. Back to Circus Circus to freshen up before work.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 1: Sat Oct 24 (3 PM) → Mon Oct 26 (10 AM)<br>• Bell desk holds bags before check-in<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Deuce stop out front. Fontainebleau is a 10-minute walk across the street.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Drop bags on arrival, then rest here 3–6 PM before the overnight bus.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.165,36.1376,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Fontainebleau</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon 26: Hotel switch, early night</b><br>10:00 — Check out; move bags across to Fontainebleau's bell desk (10 min walk). Check-in from 3 PM.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 2: Mon Oct 26 (3 PM) → Thu Oct 29 (10 AM)<br>• Conference venue<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Sahara monorail station is about a 10-minute walk.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Weeknights here start at 9 PM, so the plans nearby are short and easy.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1578,36.1371,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Wynn &amp; Encore</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Mon 26: Hotel switch, early night</b><br>9:00 PM — Optional easy stroll through Wynn &amp; Encore. Otherwise sleep; you were on a bus last night.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Flower displays and the carousel sculptures in the lobby<br>• Calm, beautiful walk-through<br><br><b>Get there:</b> About 8 minutes' walk from Fontainebleau.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> An easy Monday-night stroll if you have energy after the bus.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1657,36.1265,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Tue 27 · High Roller night ride</name><description>Free after 9 PM</description><Placemark><name>1. High Roller &amp; LINQ</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue 27: High Roller night ride</b><br>9:00 PM — Monorail from Sahara station to Harrah's/The LINQ.<br>9:30 — High Roller night ride (30 min). Book ahead.<br>10:15 — Walk the LINQ Promenade, grab a late bite.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• 550-ft observation wheel; one slow 30-minute rotation<br>• Glass cabins, views of the whole lit-up Strip<br>• LINQ Promenade: bars, shops, street food<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Monorail to Harrah's/The LINQ station (about 10 min from Sahara station).<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Tuesday it runs until 11:30 PM, so board by about 10:30. Smooth and slow, not a thrill ride.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1682,36.1176,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Fontainebleau</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Tue 27: High Roller night ride</b><br>11:30 — Monorail back (runs until 2 AM).<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 2: Mon Oct 26 (3 PM) → Thu Oct 29 (10 AM)<br>• Conference venue<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Sahara monorail station is about a 10-minute walk.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Weeknights here start at 9 PM, so the plans nearby are short and easy.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1578,36.1371,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Wed 28 · Old Vegas on Fremont</name><description>Free after 9 PM</description><Placemark><name>1. Fremont Street Experience</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 28: Old Vegas on Fremont</b><br>9:00 PM — Deuce north to Fremont Street Experience.<br>9:30 — Canopy light shows, old casinos, live music on the street.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• LED canopy light shows overhead each hour in the evening<br>• Old Vegas casinos, street performers, live music<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Deuce north from the Strip, about 20 minutes.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Wednesday 9 PM onward is perfect: it stays busy until late.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.144,36.1707,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Fontainebleau</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Wed 28: Old Vegas on Fremont</b><br>11:30 — Deuce back; it runs 24 hours.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 2: Mon Oct 26 (3 PM) → Thu Oct 29 (10 AM)<br>• Conference venue<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Sahara monorail station is about a 10-minute walk.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Weeknights here start at 9 PM, so the plans nearby are short and easy.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1578,36.1371,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Thu 29 · South Strip walk</name><description>Free after 6 PM</description><Placemark><name>1. Westgate</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu 29: South Strip walk</b><br>10:00 — Check out of Fontainebleau. Bags to Westgate (short cab or bell desk help). Check-in from 3 PM.<br>10:00 — Monorail back. Confirm your Saturday tour pickup tonight.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 3: Thu Oct 29 (3 PM) → Sat Oct 31 (before 10 AM)<br>• Has its own monorail station<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Monorail from the hotel; Deuce on Las Vegas Blvd (10 min walk).<br><br><b>Tip:</b> On Saturday, check out at 6 AM and leave bags with the bell desk for the day.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1522,36.1361,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. South Strip</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu 29: South Strip walk</b><br>6:30 PM — Monorail from Westgate to MGM Grand. Walk New York-New York, Excalibur, Luxor's beam.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• New York-New York skyline &amp; Brooklyn Bridge<br>• Excalibur castle<br>• Luxor pyramid and its sky beam<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Monorail to MGM Grand station, then walk south.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Thursday evening: fun free photos, all walkable.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1746,36.1023,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Sphere</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Thu 29: South Strip walk</b><br>8:30 — Optional: see the Exosphere glowing on Metallica night (crowds).<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• The Wizard of Oz at Sphere: 75 min, huge 360° screen, wind and scent effects<br>• Exosphere: the outside of the ball lights up with animations every evening<br>• Halloween activities in the atrium for Oz shows Oct 30 – Nov 1<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Monorail to Harrah's/LINQ, then a 10-minute walk; or Deuce to the Venetian.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Book a Friday 3–4 PM showing and arrive 30 minutes early. No late entry.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1622,36.1207,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Fri 30 · Magic Mountains + Sphere</name><description>Free after 11 AM</description><Placemark><name>1. Welcome to Fabulous Las Vegas sign</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri 30: Magic Mountains + Sphere</b><br>11:15 — Cab from Westgate, driver waits: Welcome sign photo stop.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• The classic 1959 sign<br>• Free; short photo line<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Stop on the way to Seven Magic Mountains (same cab ride).<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Midday lines are usually shorter than at sunset.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1728,36.082,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Seven Magic Mountains</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri 30: Magic Mountains + Sphere</b><br>12:00 — Seven Magic Mountains, about 45 minutes. Bring water.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Seven towers of stacked neon-painted boulders, each over 30 ft tall<br>• Art by Ugo Rondinone in the open desert<br>• Free, open any time<br><br><b>Get there:</b> No transit. Uber about 30 minutes each way; ask the driver to wait or book them for the return.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> No restrooms and no phone pickups out there, so never let the cab leave without a return plan. Bring water.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.2705,35.8385,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Sphere</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri 30: Magic Mountains + Sphere</b><br>2:30 — The Wizard of Oz at Sphere, 3–4 PM showing. Halloween activities in the atrium.<br>6:30 — Watch the Exosphere's evening show, dinner nearby.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• The Wizard of Oz at Sphere: 75 min, huge 360° screen, wind and scent effects<br>• Exosphere: the outside of the ball lights up with animations every evening<br>• Halloween activities in the atrium for Oz shows Oct 30 – Nov 1<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Monorail to Harrah's/LINQ, then a 10-minute walk; or Deuce to the Venetian.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Book a Friday 3–4 PM showing and arrive 30 minutes early. No late entry.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1622,36.1207,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Westgate</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Fri 30: Magic Mountains + Sphere</b><br>9:30 — Early night: tour pickup is about 6:30 AM.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 3: Thu Oct 29 (3 PM) → Sat Oct 31 (before 10 AM)<br>• Has its own monorail station<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Monorail from the hotel; Deuce on Las Vegas Blvd (10 min walk).<br><br><b>Tip:</b> On Saturday, check out at 6 AM and leave bags with the bell desk for the day.]]></description><styleUrl>#sff4fa3</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1522,36.1361,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Sat 31 · Grand Canyon West, then fly</name><description>Free all day · flight 11:59 PM</description><Placemark><name>1. Westgate</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 31: Grand Canyon West, then fly</b><br>6:00 — Check out; bags to Westgate bell desk. Small backpack only on the tour.<br>5:30 — Back in Vegas. Collect bags.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Hotel 3: Thu Oct 29 (3 PM) → Sat Oct 31 (before 10 AM)<br>• Has its own monorail station<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Monorail from the hotel; Deuce on Las Vegas Blvd (10 min walk).<br><br><b>Tip:</b> On Saturday, check out at 6 AM and leave bags with the bell desk for the day.]]></description><styleUrl>#sffb547</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1522,36.1361,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Grand Canyon West</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 31: Grand Canyon West, then fly</b><br>6:30 — Tour pickup (spot set by your operator).<br>10:30 — Eagle Point, Skywalk, Guano Point.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Skywalk: glass bridge 4,000 ft above the canyon floor<br>• Eagle Point: a rock that looks like an eagle<br>• Guano Point: the best wide views on the West Rim<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Bus tour from Las Vegas, about 2.5 hours each way.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Phones aren't allowed on the Skywalk (free lockers), so take photos at Guano Point.]]></description><styleUrl>#sffb547</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-113.8108,36.0119,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. Hoover Dam</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 31: Grand Canyon West, then fly</b><br>~3:30 — Hoover Dam bridge photo stop on the way back.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Walk the Memorial Bridge pedestrian path, high above the dam<br>• Nevada–Arizona state line<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Photo stop on your Grand Canyon tour.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Only small bags pass the dam checkpoint.]]></description><styleUrl>#sffb547</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-114.7377,36.016,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Bellagio Fountains</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 31: Grand Canyon West, then fly</b><br>7:00 — Halloween night on the Strip: costumes everywhere. Last fountain show.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Fountain shows set to music, every 15 minutes after dark<br>• Conservatory: free seasonal fall garden display inside<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Deuce to Bellagio/Caesars stop.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Watch from the bridge in front of Paris, or from the Eiffel Tower deck.]]></description><styleUrl>#sffb547</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1767,36.1126,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Harry Reid Airport (LAS)</name><description><![CDATA[<b>Sat 31: Grand Canyon West, then fly</b><br>9:15 — Cab to the airport for the 11:59 PM flight.<br><br><b>See:</b><br>• Arrive Sat Oct 24, 10:00 AM<br>• Depart Sat Oct 31, 11:59 PM<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Uber/Lyft to the Strip in about 15–20 minutes.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> On the last night, be at the airport by about 9:30 PM.]]></description><styleUrl>#sffb547</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1537,36.084,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder><Folder><name>Extras · if time</name><Placemark><name>STRAT SkyPod</name><description><![CDATA[<b>See:</b><br>• Indoor/outdoor observation decks 800+ ft up<br><br><b>Get there:</b> 10-minute walk from Fontainebleau or Westgate.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> If time. Skip the thrill rides on the top; the decks themselves are calm.]]></description><styleUrl>#sx</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-115.1566,36.1475,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Hollywood Sign</name><description><![CDATA[<b>See:</b><br>• You can't walk up to the letters; view it from Hollywood &amp; Highland or Griffith<br><br><b>Get there:</b> Seen from Hollywood &amp; Highland on your route.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Clearest in late-afternoon light.]]></description><styleUrl>#sx</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.3215,34.1341,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Griffith Observatory</name><description><![CDATA[<b>See:</b><br>• The closest postcard view of the Hollywood Sign<br>• Free entry, city views<br><br><b>Get there:</b> B Line to Vermont/Sunset, then the DASH Observatory bus.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Skip on this trip unless Universal finishes early; it costs about 90 minutes.]]></description><styleUrl>#sx</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.3004,34.1184,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>Venice Beach</name><description><![CDATA[<b>See:</b><br>• Boardwalk, skate park, Muscle Beach<br><br><b>Get there:</b> 2 miles south of the pier along the beach path.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Only if you reach Santa Monica early.]]></description><styleUrl>#sx</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-118.4695,33.985,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Folder></Document></kml>